-- Events under `dom` (backend.md §15.3; research 36 §2.7, §4.6). A
-- delegated event is one property write, `$$click`, which `p` rewrites
-- only when the handler changed; a handler that takes a payload also gets
-- its extractor, `Html.targetValue` imported from the vocabulary module,
-- or the runtime's `identity` for the event itself. A declaration's
-- `preventDefault` is a flag on the node. An event that is not delegated
-- gets one stable listener at mount, which reads the handler the node
-- holds when it fires. A node with a handler records the mount context
-- when there is one, for `Html.map`. This is a `--library` build, which
-- has no program start: each kind registers the names it delegates.
import Html exposing (Html)


type Msg
    = Clicked Int
    | Typed String
    | Sent
    | Focused
    | Down Html.Event


pub view : Int -> Html Msg
view n =
    <form onSubmit={Sent}>
        <button onClick={Clicked n}>go</button>
        <input onInput={Typed} onFocus={Focused} onKeyDown={Down} />
    </form>
